  "foaf:name": "Blue Guard Alliance TCI",
  "sdo:name": "Blue Guard Alliance TCI",
  "sdo:description": "Blue Guard Alliance TCI will transform fisheries governance in the Turks and Caicos Island, a SIDS through climate-resilient, community inclusive management. The project deploys digital data collection, VMS, e-licensing and will establishes the Caribbean&#x27;s first national environmental DNA (eDNA) biodiversity observatory aligned with OBON standards. Six components deliver: (1) real-time VMS and catch data; (2) eDNA-based species and habitat mapping for MPAs and TACs; (3) modernized fisheries legislation and operationalized Fisheries Management Plan; (4) Local Fisheries Management Committees and ocean literacy; (5) blue economy pilots (lobster casitas, FADs, traceability); (6) regional knowledge exchange. Targeting queen conch, spiny lobster and finfish upon which 40,000+ people depend, the project co-produces data-driven solutions with fishers, women, youth and agencies, positioning TCI as a SIDS leader in technology-enabled, equitable ocean stewardship under FishSCORE 2030 and OBON.",
  "sdo:location": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK)",
  "sdo:identifier": "11.1",
